# Everything the image builds for itself, plus everything it must never carry.
#
# The two `node_modules` are reinstalled from the lockfiles inside the image, so copying the host's
# would only import whatever architecture this laptop happens to be. `dist/` and `web/dist/` are
# built in the first stage from source. `data/` is a bind mount at runtime — baking a copy of it in
# would ship somebody's run screenshots inside the image. `.env` holds the API key.

node_modules
web/node_modules
dist
web/dist
data
.env
.git
.gitignore
.superpowers
tests
docs
scripts

# Not build inputs, and a stale one confuses `docker build` context caching more than it helps.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
deploy.sh
README.md
